-- title:
--   Finitely many places descend to a finite constant field
-- statement:
--   Let $K'$ be a field of characteristic a prime $\ell$ in which every element $a$ satisfies $a^{\ell^{n}}=a$ for some $n>0$, and let $F'$ be a $K'$-algebra which is a field such that some $x\in F'$ is transcendental over $K'$ with $F'$ finite-dimensional over $K'(x)$. Assume $F'/K'$ is a curve in the sense of `IsCurveOver`: every nonzero $f\in F'$ has a degree-zero divisor recording the orders $\mathrm{ord}_v f$ at all places, every place has residue field finite over $K'$, and $\Omega_{F'/K'}$ is free of rank one over $F'$; assume further `ConstantsAreBase K' F'`, i.e. the Riemann–Roch space $L(0)$ is exactly the image of $K'$ in $F'$. Then for every finite set $W$ of places of $F'/K'$ there are a finite field $K$ and a field $F$, with algebra maps $K\to K'$, $K\to F$, $F\to F'$, $K\to F'$ forming compatible scalar towers $K\to K'\to F'$ and $K\to F\to F'$, with $F'$ integral over $F$, $F/K$ again a curve in the above sense and essentially of finite type over $K$, such that the $F$-subalgebra of $F'$ generated by the image of $K'$ is all of $F'$, `ConstantsAreBase K F` holds, and for each $w\in W$, writing $v$ for the place of $F/K$ obtained by viewing $w$ as a place of $F'/K$ and restricting to $F$, the finite set of places of $F'/K'$ lying over $v$ in this sense is $\{w\}$ and $\operatorname{finrank}_K \kappa(v)=\operatorname{finrank}_{K'}\kappa(w)$.
--
--   This is the classical statement that finitely many places of a function field over an algebraic extension of $\mathbb{F}_\ell$ are already defined over a finite constant field, remain inert in the constant field extension, and keep their residue degree. It is used by [`AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.exists_finite_constantField_form_pullbackConstants_eq`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.Divisor.exists_finite_constantField_form_pullbackConstants_eq) to write an arbitrary divisor of $F'/K'$ as the pullback of a divisor over a finite constant field.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_exists_finite_constantField_form_fiberConstants_eq_singleton.lean

